      "id": "1079gcd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.5 Climate"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tamil Nadu has a tropical climate. Unlike most of India, Tamil Nadu receives most of its rainfall from the Northeast Monsoon (October–December) rather than the Southwest Monsoon, because the Western Ghats block the Southwest Monsoon. The state has four seasons: Winter (Jan–Feb), Summer (Mar–May), Southwest Monsoon (Jun–Sep), and Northeast Monsoon (Oct–Dec).",
      "id": "f9uwpym"
    },
    {
      "id": "om46tce",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Average annual rainfall: ~945 mm",
        "Highest rainfall zone: Nilgiris (over 2,500 mm)",
        "Lowest rainfall zone: Ramanathapuram and Thoothukudi (below 600 mm)",
        "Chennai receives most rain from Northeast Monsoon"
      ]
    },
